    {
      "id": "king-john/sceneIII_16.3/p@76911",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "KING JOHN.\n[To the Bastard] Cousin, away for England! Haste before,\nAnd, ere our coming, see thou shake the bags\nOf hoarding abbots; imprison’d angels\nSet at liberty. The fat ribs of peace\nMust by the hungry now be fed upon.\nUse our commission in his utmost force.",
